# go-lighter examples — environment template.
# Copy to .env (git-ignored). NEVER commit real keys.
#
# Lighter authenticates with API keys bound to an account index (not with the
# L1 wallet key). The three variables follow the desk's credential convention
# (<EXCHANGE>_API_KEY / _SECRET_KEY / _PASSPHRASE):
#   API_KEY     account index (integer; sub-accounts have their own index)
#   SECRET_KEY  private key(s) of the API key(s): 40-byte hex, optional 0x
#               prefix; several keys separated by commas (v2.0 key pool)
#   PASSPHRASE  API key index(es) 2..254, comma separated, same order as the
#               private keys
# API keys are registered on the account with a changePubKey transaction signed
# by the L1 wallet (see the official Python SDK examples/system_setup.py).
#
# Lighter has no testnet credentials available to this desk: the trading
# example runs on MAINNET with real funds. Keep LIGHTER_ALLOW_LIVE=0 unless
# you really mean it.

LIGHTER_PERPETUALS_API_KEY=
LIGHTER_PERPETUALS_SECRET_KEY=
LIGHTER_PERPETUALS_PASSPHRASE=

# Safety gate of the order-sending example.
LIGHTER_ALLOW_LIVE=0

# Optional knobs.
LIGHTER_TESTNET=0
LIGHTER_SYMBOL=ETH
LIGHTER_NOTIONAL=12
